Patch 43. In the series since 2026-10-17, after patch 42.

ReXApp (src/ui/rex_app.cpp) puts its config, <app>.toml (which the settings dialog saves), and
its logs next to the executable. On Android the executable's folder is the app's native library
folder, read-only or inside the APK, so neither could be written. There they go with the user
data (user_data_root, by default the user folder, which the Android main points at the app's
internal storage). An app can still move them (OnConfigurePaths, OnConfigureLogging). Every
other platform is unchanged.

Test: the SDK builds for Android and desktop. On the POCO X7 the game's settings are in the app's
internal files, and its logs in the folder the game chooses, with no write error (the game sets
its own folders; these defaults matter to apps that do not).

